{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","role":"collection","externalID":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Google Analytics","anchor":"Sending-to-Google-Analytics"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for a Google Analytics 4 stream in one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call. It checks the measurement ID and the API secret, and posts to the Measurement Protocol’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/mp\/collect"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the region ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion"},{"type":"text","text":") with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each batch to the Measurement Protocol’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 25 events and 100 KB a request. A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"The API secret stays on a server","type":"heading","anchor":"The-API-secret-stays-on-a-server"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol takes only requests that carry one of the stream’s API secrets, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anyone holding that secret can send events to the property. Google’s docs say not to expose it in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an app, and an app’s binary can be read by anyone who installs it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the whole module is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, where a server runs. An app for iOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iPadOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS or Mac Catalyst that calls the factory, or names the encoder, fails"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to compile. A Mac app, AppKit or SwiftUI, compiles the factory as a Mac server does, but the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory refuses it at run time: it throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"process’s main bundle is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".app"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".appex"},{"type":"text","text":". Nothing stops a Mac app from building an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" with this encoder and an endpoint it writes itself, secret and all, so don’t."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The secret is also in the query of every request’s URL. Don’t log the destination, its requests or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a transport’s URLs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","isActive":true},{"text":" for an empty measurement ID, for one that isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G-"},{"text":" followed by uppercase letters and digits, and for an empty API secret. The region has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".global"},{"text":" is Google’s default endpoint, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".eu"},{"text":" has Google collect the data in the EU.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Getting an app’s events to Google Analytics","type":"heading","anchor":"Getting-an-apps-events-to-Google-Analytics"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app’s events reach Google Analytics through a server of yours: the app sends them there, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the server makes this destination and hands it the records. Traffluent doesn’t provide that server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yet. TraffluentCollector receives an app’s batches, but it doesn’t forward them to Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analytics, and Traffluent has no decoder that turns a collector batch back into records."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Until it does, the server’s job is:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read each event the app sent (its name, version, identifier, timestamp, properties and session)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decode it into the same "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type the app tracked, from a module the app and the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Remake its "},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"EventRecord(id:event:timestamp:sourceLocation:context:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app’s identifier and timestamp, and a context whose "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the app’s session."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand each batch of records to the destination’s "},{"code":"receive(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t track the events again through a "},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the server. That tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would give every event the server’s own session, so every user of the app would arrive in Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analytics as one "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A server that tracks its own events, rather than an app’s, uses a tracker as any app does:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)","\/\/ A server tracking its own events: its sessions are the server's.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: googleAnalytics)"]},{"level":3,"text":"What Google Analytics receives","type":"heading","anchor":"What-Google-Analytics-receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request holds one client’s events, as the Measurement Protocol takes one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, written as the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"halves of its UUID in decimal, joined by a period, the form the Measurement Protocol asks for. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, in a request of its own. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter is the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, so Google Analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"groups the session’s events, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s timestamp. Every request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends ad consent as denied, so Google uses none of the events for advertising."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", user properties, location, IP address, device or user agent is sent, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"advertising identifier. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and standard context aren’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent either. Google Analytics counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports, and so is each record sent without a session."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engagement_time_msec"},{"text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t measure engagement. Without it the events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"don’t count toward engagement time or engaged sessions, and the Realtime and Users reports can show","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no users while events arrive. Check the event counts, not the user counts, to see that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination works.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and become the event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"params"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans, so a nested value is spread into a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart_size"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags_0"},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":" is left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Records sent twice","type":"heading","anchor":"Records-sent-twice"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics can’t tell a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"repeat from a new event, and counts every one it receives. A record is sent more than once when a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request is retried after Google stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancelled batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each such record is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted twice in Google Analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Records left out","type":"heading","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name, or a parameter’s name, is longer than 40 bytes, doesn’t start with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letter, or holds anything but letters, numbers and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Google Analytics keeps (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_start"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first_visit"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"text":" and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its reserved names), or takes only from an app stream (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_view"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_impression"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in_app_purchase"},{"text":");","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a parameter Google Analytics keeps (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"firebase_"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ga_"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"google_"},{"type":"text","text":" prefix) or named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which the encoder writes;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one of more than 25 parameters, counting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", or with a string longer than 100 bytes;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one tracked more than 71 hours before the batch is encoded, or more than 15 minutes after it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one whose timestamp has no microseconds form;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one too large for a request."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics wouldn’t refuse such an event: it answers 2xx either way. Under its default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaxed validation it stores the event without the parameter that breaks a rule, or under a name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it never checked, so the report would hold an event other than the one tracked. The encoder leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the record out and reports it instead. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of up to 500"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":". The encoder logs a notice for each event and property of the plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named as Google Analytics refuses when the destination is made; rename such an event or property,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raising the event’s version, to send it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"What the Measurement Protocol doesn’t report","type":"heading","anchor":"What-the-Measurement-Protocol-doesnt-report"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, including one it can’t read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose events it doesn’t store. A wrong measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored, so check the property’s Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. Google’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation server, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/debug\/mp\/collect"},{"type":"text","text":", checks a body’s shape but not the measurement ID or the API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"secret, so a body it accepts can still be stored nowhere. A record older than 72 hours is stored as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if it happened 72 hours ago, so the encoder leaves out one older than 71 hours, the hour to spare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the request to reach Google and clocks that disagree. A request is encoded once and retried as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it is, so the encoder gives each request a deadline 71 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request still failing by then isn’t sent again: the destination drops the whole request, its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"younger records too, and reports it on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or Segment, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Google Analytics receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding"]}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticssetuperror","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"measurementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", authenticated by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"apiSecret","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/googleanalytics(measurementid:apisecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"googleAnalytics"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"measurementID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"apiSecret"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB6RegionO","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","text":"Date"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB10SetupErrorO","text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","text":"URLSessionTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","title":"BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsencodingerror","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError/appBundle":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The process is an app or an app extension: its main bundle is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".app"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".appex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory. The factory is compiled for macOS so a server written for it can run there, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mac app compiles it too, but an app ships the API secret to everyone who installs it, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding the secret can send events to the property. Send the app’s events to a relay"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text